cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below. The
  version is the package version in pyproject.toml; no release tag has been
  cut for it, so cite the commit you used, especially when you depend on a
  specific result (the daily job keeps committing data).
type: software
title: "Joint SPX/VIX Calibration System"
abstract: >-
  An end-of-day research system that fits one Heston model jointly to the
  SPX option smile and the four Cboe VIX indices (VIX9D, VIX, VIX3M, VIX6M);
  VIX options are a research leg, not in the objective. Heston and Bates
  pricing by the Lewis (2001) contour integral with a Black-Scholes control
  variate, exact VIX index and VIX futures formulas, a session-dated and
  look-ahead-gated SPX option-chain pipeline, the joint calibration
  (multi-start least squares with an analytic Jacobian, identifiability
  diagnostics, a sigma-box profile and a rough Heston comparison), an SVI
  surface certified free of butterfly and calendar arbitrage on a numerical
  grid, every model scored against the quoted bid-ask on quotes it was not
  fitted to, a Treasury zero curve, a delta-hedged straddle backtest priced
  mark-to-model with bootstrap intervals, deflated Sharpe ratios and
  exposure-matched nulls (it reports a negative result), a forward ledger at
  executable prices, and the static dashboard published at
  https://navnoorbawa.me.
authors:
